# Django
#
# Every SQLite artefact, not just the main file. The old entry listed only
# `db.sqlite3` and `db.sqlite3-journal`, so the `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars were
# not covered -- and a 4 MB `db.sqlite3-wal` holding uncommitted pages of the real
# scan database was committed and pushed. `*.sqlite3*` catches all of them.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-journal
staticfiles/
media/
*.log

# Local database backups
#
# `backend/backups/` holds timestamped SQLite snapshots. One of these was a 79 MB
# demo database and ended up in a commit, which is why pushes started warning
# about files over GitHub's 50 MB limit.
backend/backups/
backups/

